{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdLociDensity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdLociDensity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdUniquenessComplete","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdDivisor","lean:module:QOU.Common.PeriodicDense","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Complex.Circle"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdLociDensity.phiBProd_uniqueUpToScalar_of_normalForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdLociDensity.phiBProd_uniqueUpToScalar_of_normalForm","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhiBProdLociDensity.lean#L153-L199","doc":"**`phiBProd` uniqueness up to scalar — loci discharged.** Any substrate `FaddeevPhi` +\n`FaddeevPhiStripGrowth` solution `Φ₁` in meromorphic normal form is proportional to `phiBProd`.\nThe dense periodicity loci are constructed explicitly and their density is proved from the\ncountability of the prefactor and `phiBProd`-zero sets. The **only** remaining hypothesis is the\nhonest regularity `MeromorphicNFOn Φ₁`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdLociDensity.dualPrefactor_zeros_countable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdLociDensity.dualPrefactor_zeros_countable","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhiBProdLociDensity.lean#L129-L151","doc":"The dual quasi-period prefactor's zero set is countable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdLociDensity.primaryPrefactor_zeros_countable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdLociDensity.primaryPrefactor_zeros_countable","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhiBProdLociDensity.lean#L112-L127","doc":"The primary quasi-period prefactor's zero set is countable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdLociDensity.phiBProd_shift_zeros_countable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdLociDensity.phiBProd_shift_zeros_countable","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhiBProdLociDensity.lean#L104-L110","doc":"The zero set of `z ↦ phiBProd b (z + c)` is countable (a translate of `phiBProd`'s zeros). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdLociDensity.phiBProd_zeros_countable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdLociDensity.phiBProd_zeros_countable","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhiBProdLociDensity.lean#L93-L102","doc":"**`phiBProd`'s zero set is countable**: `phiBProd = num·den⁻¹`, so it vanishes only where\n`num` or `den` does, both countable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdLociDensity.den_zeros_countable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdLociDensity.den_zeros_countable","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhiBProdLociDensity.lean#L82-L91","doc":"The denominator product's zero set is countable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdLociDensity.num_zeros_countable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdLociDensity.num_zeros_countable","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhiBProdLociDensity.lean#L71-L80","doc":"The numerator product's zero set is countable (union over `k` of the factor lattices). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdLociDensity.denFactor_zeros_countable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdLociDensity.denFactor_zeros_countable","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhiBProdLociDensity.lean#L49-L69","doc":"Each denominator factor's zero set is countable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdLociDensity.numFactor_zeros_countable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdLociDensity.numFactor_zeros_countable","kind":"theorem","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhiBProdLociDensity.lean#L33-L47","doc":"Each numerator factor's zero set is countable (a discrete `ℤ`-lattice). ","signatureChunk":0}]}